                                <DTC ID="DTCC2471A0" OID="935fe784-cc1f-4add-a226-4f82fc2f2e37">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2471A0</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6582688</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2471A0</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1021462782">Monitoring of wheel direction differences. Faulty wheel not assignable</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_352656679">The fault is set if the detected rotation directions of two wheels are not the same and two wheels have no direction OR if the detected rotation directions of two wheels are opposite of the detected rotation directions of the other two wheels. The rotation direction can only be logged with directional WSS.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_2027532450">1.) At least one wheel speed sensor is mounted in wrong direction. 2.) At least one wrong wheel speed sensor is mounted. 3.) At least one wheel speed sensor is wrongly connected.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2471A1" OID="58fcc7cb-1329-4a1a-ad65-8578314ac207">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2471A1</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6582689</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2471A1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1174560566">Monitoring of wheel speed differences. Faulty wheel not assignable</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1440893576">This failure is set if the difference between maximum and minimum wheel speed related to vehicle speed exceeds a calculated threshold. This threshold is depending on vehicle speed and current system mode. A generic fault is set, if the faulty wheel is not always the same. 1.) ESP Mode: For vehicle speeds lower than a specific value %{ 5.56 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_v_Switch5 }% the failure threshold is an absolute value %{ 1.4 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo5/SspWss_MonVdiff_v_SREF_perc }%. Above this vehicle speed the failure threshold is a relative value %{ 5 | % | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo5 }%. 2.) ABS and backup-EBD Mode: For vehicle speeds lower than a specific value %{ 27.8 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_v_Switch6 }% the failure threshold is an absolute value %{ 1.7 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo6/SspWss_MonVdiff_v_SREF_perc }%. Above this vehicle speed the failure threshold is a relative value %{ 6 | % | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo6 }%.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1279227902">1.) Wrong tyre size. 2.) Wrong pulse wheel toothcount. 3.) The WSS is not correctly mounted, so that no signal is induced in sensor element. 4.) The WSS is dislodged from bracket, so that no signal is induced in sensor element.  5.) The airgap between sensor and encoding wheel is too big to induce sufficient signal in sensor element. 6.) Malfunction of sensor internal logic. 7.) Tone wheel not mounted correctly or demagnetized. 8.) The WSS signal is disturbed by loose contact. 9.) The WSS signal is disturbed by open circuit in the WSS line.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC246AA2" OID="463a83a0-471d-4dda-ba06-0861d43130fc">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC246AA2</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6580898</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C246AA2</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
