                                <DTC ID="DTCC2455A0" OID="806fde7f-d856-4b07-8585-857ee1be13df">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2455A0</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6575520</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2455A0</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1172547308">Wss swapped front axle</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_43531256">"The yaw rate calculated from steering angle and the yaw rates calculated from the wheel speed sensors at both axles are compared. If the yaw rates fit, positive integrals (IvGiVrVZFA and IvGiVrVZRA) are calculated, but if the negative values fit, the integrals will become negative. A fault is determined if the integral value IvGiVrVZFA is negative and a threshold of %{ 1.5708|rad|0| IvorwaertsSw2# }% is exceeded. This fault will cause a release test in the following ignition cycle to assure that the sensors are build in correctly. The conditions for release are IvGiVrVZFA AND IvGiVrVZRA are &gt;= %{ 3.14 | rad | 0 | IvorwaertsSw3# }%.Alternative monitoring without usage of Sas and Yrs, If switches %{ true|-|1| FS_Mbp_WssSignType_WssOnly# }%  &amp;&amp; %{ false|-|1| FS_Mbp_WssSignType_WssOnly# }%:During stable cornering the wheel speeds are in a defined order which is checked by this monitoring. If the order shows a fault pattern within stable cornering until the failure counter timer_WssSign reaches 125, the fault is set. If an EBD intervention is happening during stable cornering, it is assumed to be a misintervention due to swapped Wss at the rear axle and failure word Wss_SignRA is set. If no EBD misintervention has happened, the failure word Wss_SignFA is set."</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1414437169">Wheel speed sensors are swapped at front axle.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2452A8" OID="9624da6c-2164-4a33-9cef-26d474075b01">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2452A8</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574760</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2452A8</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_316111223">Temporary system degradation due to multiple WSS fault suspicion.</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1961421221">The failure is set if ABS and EBD are released by diagnosis and system management while these controllers are not able to work because required input signals are not available with sufficient quality. This is the case if WSS input signals from less than two wheels are available without assigned fault or fault suspicion for min. 0,5 s consecutively (e.g. the failure is set if at least three WSS show an implausible behavior for 0,5 s). 			If detection is occurring during an ABS or EBD control on the rear axle, the failure setting is shifted until control on rear axle is finished.			The implausibility can be due to different reasons:			a)	fault assigned to any wheel (ModeFail, SupplyGnd, SupplyHigh, LineHigh, LineGnd, LineUndef, TestFailure, DmaBufNoise, WrongSens, NoEdge, VdaParityBitFail, MonRange, SignalLost, MonVDiff, MonMissingTeeth, MonNoise), or			b)	implausible WSS signal detected temporarily due to				1.) wheel speed is higher than a specific threshold %{ 82.23 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_SiS_vMax }% for min. 0,5 s.				2.) wheel speed stays at zero after drive off afterwards the vehicle velocity increases a specific threshold %{ 3.3 | m/s | 1 |   }%.				3.) wheel speed drops to zero while the vehicle is faster than a specific velocity threshold %{ 3.3 | m/s | 2 | MAX(MAX((SspWss_vDOLO_CheckFailLower*((48/2)/(AnzahlZaehne_VA/Abrollumfang_VA))),SspWss_vDOLO_CheckFailLower),SspWss_v_DOHI_Offset)}% and the vehicle does not decelerate below the vehicle speed that was present when the initial wheel speed drop occurred.				4.) wheel acceleration is implausible high, the wheel jerk is implausible high or edges and time information do not match at low speed.				5.) wheel speed differs from other wheel speeds more than a calculated threshold and a varying duration. The threshold is depending on vehicle speed and current system mode, the debounce time is depending on drive situation, current system mode and project specific threshold.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1222111073">Multiple not plausible or invalid WSS signals were detected.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2455A1" OID="47688140-450b-4164-96a4-ba4d4ff65a74">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2455A1</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6575521</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2455A1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1219230359">Wss swapped rear axle</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1072423266">"This monitoring detects wrongly mounted wheel speed sensors at rear axle. The yaw rate calculated from steering angle and the yaw rates calculated from the wheel speed sensors at both axles are compared. If the yaw rates fit, positive integrals (IvGiVrVZFA and IvGiVrVZRA) are calculated, but if the negative values fit, the integrals will become negative. A fault is determined if the integral value IvGiVrVZRA is negative and a threshold of %{ 1.5708|rad|0| IvorwaertsSw2# }% is exceeded. This fault will cause a release test in the following ignition cycle to assure that the sensors are build in correctly. The conditions for release are IvGiVrVZFA &gt;= %{ 3.14 | rad | 0 | IvorwaertsSw3# }% AND IvGiVrVZRA &gt;= %{ 3.14 | rad | 0 | IvorwaertsSw3# }% .Alternative monitoring without usage of Sas and Yrs, if switches FS_Mbp_WssSignType_WssOnly == true &amp;&amp; IUMPR_MbpSignMonitoring_Active == false:During stable cornering the wheel speeds are in a defined order which is checked by this monitoring. If the order shows a fault pattern within stable cornering until the failure counter timer_WssSign reaches 125, the fault is set. If an EBD intervention is happening during stable cornering, it is assumed to be a misintervention due to swapped Wss at the rear axle and failure word Wss_SignRA is set. If no EBD misintervention has happened, the failure word Wss_SignFA is set."</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_340195454">Wheel speed sensors are swapped at rear axle.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC245FAA" OID="2e693403-fb03-4dab-ba1d-14bb8e213a89">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC245FAA</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6578090</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C245FAA</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1355864619">All Sensor cluster AYS , AXS and YRS failures</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1940793464">Integrated yawrate sensor signal fault (SMI7 sensor). Possible contributors: SPITransError, GeneralYrsFault</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1951193710">Multiple or a sporadical failure leads to extended yawrate signal freeze.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2456A9" OID="d75eb93b-e36e-4943-ad0b-c8714cc9ed9d">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2456A9</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6575785</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2456A9</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1796540517">This monitoring detects a wrong sign of yaw rate signal. The measured yaw rate and the model yaw rate calculated from the steering angle are compared. During forward driving these signals must have the same sign. If the measured yaw rate  fits to the model yaw rate from steering angle,  positive integrals (Ivorwaerts,IvGiVrFA,IvGiVrRA ) is calculated but if the negative value fits the integral will become negative. A fault is determined if the integral value of the measured yaw rate(Ivorwaerts) is negative and smaller than %{ -0.5236 | rad | 2 | IvorwaertsSw1# }%,  forward driving is recognized either by reaching a speed threshold close to maximum possible reverse speed %{ 19.5 | m/s | 1 | P_vFzRefVorwSw # }% or by intelligent wheel speed sensors direction information and the integrals of the model yaw rates obtained from wheel speeds at front and rear axle(IvGiVrFA, IvGiVrRA) are greater than %{0.5236 | rad/s | 2 | IvorwaertsSw1#}%. This fault requires a release check in the following ignition cycle to prevent system release when the fault is still present. The conditions for release are positive integral(Ivorwaerts) &gt; +180 deg AND after that the vehicle drives faster than P_Vfric (default value: 20 m/s).</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_847645510">Wrong wiring or wrong assembly position of the sensor.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450AD" OID="0360a586-fd5d-4775-b681-c98f53dd52bf">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450AD</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574253</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450AD</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1526307451">Yaw rate signal Out of Range(High)</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_458587560">The monitoring checks for a physically plausible yaw rate and consists of following parts: 1.) YrsStandstillRange: The failure is set if the yaw rate  is more than 30Â°/s for 0.5s during first standstill after ignition ON.  2.) YrsDriveRange: The failure is set if the yaw rate  is more than 94.75Â°/s for 0.8s.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_317584101">The Yaw rate signal value is greater than the maximum value  plausible for the vehicle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450AE" OID="18e8e51e-f4a8-4378-bb53-c4e0602ab558">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450AE</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574254</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450AE</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_685622475">Yaw rate signal Out of Range(Low)</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_779135155">The monitoring checks for a physically plausible yaw rate and consists of following parts: 1.) YrsStandstillRange: The failure is set if the yaw rate  is less than -30Â°/s for 0.5s during first standstill after ignition ON.  2.) YrsDriveRange: The failure is set if the yaw rate  is less than -94.75Â°/s for 0.8s.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1332034177">The Yaw rate signal value is less than the minimum value  plausible for the vehicle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450AF" OID="1d03eeff-7098-4716-93a8-85c08f319856">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450AF</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574255</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450AF</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1190642429">The monitoring checks for a physically plausible yaw rate and consists of following parts: 1.) YrsFastOffset1: The failure is set if the yaw rate offset is higher than a specific threshold %{ 0.2622 | rad/s | 4 | P_vGiInOfsFP }%. The yaw rate offset corresponds to the slightly filtered deviation between measured yaw rate and the calculated reference yaw rate. 2.) YrsFastOffset2: The failure is set at the end of the fast compensation and if the offset is higher than a specific threshold %{ 0.1309 | rad/s | 4 | P_vGiOfsMaxFSAbgl }%. The yaw rate offset corresponds to the slightly filtered deviation between measured yaw rate and the calculated reference yaw rate. 3.) Yrs_Gain: The failure is set if the sensitiviy deviation of the yaw rate is higher than a specific threshold %{ 0.25 | | 2 | P_vGiInEmpfErr }%. The yaw rate gain is estimated by comparison of the measured yaw rate and the yaw rate calculated from steering angle and wheel speed sensors during cornering. 4.) Yrs_MonGrad: The failure is set if the signal gradient from one task cycle to another is between specific thresholds %{ 10 | deg/s | 0 | igrd_DiffvGiInUG }% %{ 23 | deg/s | 0 | igrd_DiffvGiInOG }%. The threshold increases while non-stationary driving condition. 5.) Yrs_MonRangeDriving: The failure is set if the absolute value of the yaw rate sensor signal is higher than a specific threshold %{ 94.75 | deg/s | 2 | ibed_vGiAnScndMax-idrs_DrsOffset }%. 6.) Yrs_MonRangeVehStandstill: The failure is set if the absolute value of the yaw rate sensor signal is higher than a specific threshold %{ 30 | deg/s | 0 | ibed_vGiAnFrstMax }%. 7.) Yrs_NormalOffset: The failure is set if the yaw rate offset is higher than a specific threshold %{ 0.1309 | rad/s | 4 | P_vGiOfsMaxFSAbgl }%. The yaw rate offset corresponds to the strong filtered deviation between measured yaw rate and the calculated reference yaw rate. 8.) Yrs_PlausLimVal: The failure is set if the measured and offset compensated yaw rate signal does not follow the reference yaw rate signal. If the measured yaw rate deviates more than a dynamic threshold from the reference yaw rate the quadratic value of the deviation is integrated. The dynamic threshold has a minimum value %{ 0.035 | rad/s | 3 | zvGiRefOversteering }%. The failure is set if the fault integral is higher than a specific threshold %{ 20 | deg/s | 2 | }%. 9.) Yrs_PlausSas: The fault is set if te difference between measured steering angle and model calculated value based on yaw rate signal is higher than a velocity dependent threshold. The bigger the velocity, the lower the threshold. The threshold is between two values %{ 10 | deg | 0 | }% %{ 100 | deg | 0 | }%. The deviation is recognized through three possible recognition paths evaluating stable driving conditions. This is to prevent a fault recognition due to unstable driving. The sensor - yaw rate sensor or steering angle sensor - which is showing the largest deviation to the reference yaw rate is marked as faulty. 10.) Yrs_PlausValidity: The failure is set if the measured and offset compensated yaw rate signal does not follow the reference yaw rate signal. If the deviation is higher than a dynamic threshold a failure is recognized. The dynamic threshold consists of a fix value %{ 0.04363 | rad/s | 5 | zDifvGiErrC1 }% plus situation depending values. 11.) Yrs_StandstillComp: The failure is set if the filtered yaw rate offset is higher than a specific threshold %{ 0.09163 | rad/s | 5 | P_vGiOfsStAbglMax }%. This yaw rate offset is calculated by filtering the measured yaw rate during standstill within a specific time %{ 1.52 | s | 2 | tStAbglSw }% while standstill. At drive off the offset value is checked.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_49578639">The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by sensor internal failure.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
