                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450A5" OID="e67d4fc0-3356-423b-99ca-de7126c52925">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450A5</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574245</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450A5</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1599540560">The failure is set if the deviation between measured longitudinal acceleration and longitudinal acceleration calculated by differentiating vehicle reference speed is higher than a specific threshold %{ 36 | % | 2 | fac_a_MinAxOutput*100 }% for a specific time %{ 2 | s | 0 | t_Ax_Output_Filt_Time }%. The failure is only set if vehicle velocity is higher than a specific threshold %{ 6 | m/s | 2 | MAX(v_MINAX,SspWss_v_Rad_Min_GA) }%.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_49578639">The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by sensor internal failure.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450A6" OID="dada6b89-099d-4a7e-9004-64048d028078">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450A6</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574246</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450A6</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_517797035">The monitoring consists of two parts: 1.) High acceleration monitoring: The failure is set if the longitudinal acceleration is higher than a minimum threshold %{ 0.5 | m/s^2 | 1 | AxsHighAccelerationMonitoringAddThreshold }% added by a threshold depending on velocity %{ 3.5 | m/s^2 | 1 | AxsPlausibilityMonitoringThresholdTable }% for a long time during driving. 2.) Plausibiltiy versus vehicle acceleration: The failure is set if the difference between measured longitudinal acceleration and longitudinal acceleration calculated by differentiating vehicle velocity is higher than a velocity depending threshold %{ 3.5 | m/s^2 | 1 | AxsPlausibilityMonitoringThresholdTable }%.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_49578639">The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by sensor internal failure.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450A7" OID="701f099a-be1b-4cf4-a480-3cf24e3566eb">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450A7</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574247</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450A7</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1917791704">The monitoring consists of two parts. 1.) Offset monitoring: The failure is set if the long time filtered longitudinal acceleration value called longitudinal acceleration offset is higher than a specific threshold %{ 2.25 | m/s^2 | 2 | P_axOfsLZAErr }%. Calculation of the longitudinal acceleration offset is done in this way: During normal driving for a long time a symmetrical driving situation is supposed. In this case the mean driving direction is on a plane surface and the long time filtered longitudinal acceleration should be zero. The deviation from the zero position is the longitudinal acceleration offset. The offset is stored in the eeprom over the power cycle. 2.) Missalignment monitoring: The failure is set if the difference between the stored offset value and the new learned offset value is higher than a specific threshold %{ 0.0865 | m/s^2 | 4 | P_MADError/20 }% after a specific learning distance %{ 10000 | m | 0 | (P_WegstrIAx*P_LTCAxIntCount_limit)/20 }%. If the absolute covered distance is lower than a specific threshold %{ 200000 | m | 0 | (P_WegstrIAx*P_LTCAxIntCount_limit) }% the check threshold is increased %{ 1.153 | m/s^2 | 4 | P_MADError/20 }%.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1333432061">1.) The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by sensor internal failure. 2.) The inertial sensor signal is faulty because of wrong calibration. 3.) The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by HU misalignment.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2450A8" OID="2f7e9ec7-6d61-4215-8862-39b48522b2fb">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2450A8</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6574248</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2450A8</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1558561880">The monitoring consists of two parts. 1.) Offset monitoring: The failure is set if the long time filtered lateral acceleration value called lateral acceleration offset is higher than a specific threshold %{ 2.25 | m/s^2 | 2 | ayInOfsFineErr }%. Calculation of the lateral acceleration offset is done in this way: During normal driving for a long time a symmetrical driving situation is supposed. In this case the mean driving direction is straight ahead and the long time filtered lateral acceleration should be zero. The deviation from the zero position is the lateral acceleration offset. The offset is stored in the eeprom over the power cycle. 2.) Missalignment monitoring: The failure is set if the new learned offset value has changed by more than a virtually learned offset value after a specific learning distance %{ 10000 | m | 0 | P_MAD_AyDistance }%. The virtually learned offset value corresponds to the partly compensated offset value after the specific learning distance assumed the (non compensated) virtual offset had been a specific value %{ 1.73 | m/s^2 | 4 | P_MADError }% at beginning of the monitoring interval.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1333432061">1.) The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by sensor internal failure. 2.) The inertial sensor signal is faulty because of wrong calibration. 3.) The inertial sensor signal was disturbed by HU misalignment.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC2456A4" OID="79a59533-02f2-46e3-8e35-89a1e5ed7e47">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC2456A4</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6575780</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C2456A4</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2137440368">Error passiv failure on Can 0</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_2009780776">The monitoring checks for a physically plausible lateral acceleration signal and consists of following parts:1) Monitoring during validity:By building a reference lateral acceleration from all available sensor signals - steering angle - yaw rate - lateral acceleration - wheel speed sensors - it is possible to test the lateral acceleration(Ay)-signal on plausibility. If during stable vehicle behaviour a lateral acceleration failure larger than approximately a sum of %{ 2.0 | m/sÂ² | 1 | zDifAyErrC1}% and needed increase in tolerance based on the situation occurs, the failure condition is fulfilled and a fault is recognized during straight ahead driving, when the failure counter tayFV1 reaches %{1600 | ms | 0 | tayFV1Sw * 40 }% during model validity.During cornering only the failure counterincreases and when the threshold is reached the vehicle dynamics controller will disregard the sensor information so that a false  intervention is prevented.2) Monitoring during model observability:By building a reference lateral acceleration from all available sensor signals - steering angle - yaw rate - lateral acceleration - wheel speed sensors - it is possible to test the lateral acceleration signal on plausibility. If during stable vehicle behavior a lateral acceleration failure larger than approximately %{ 2.0 | m/sÂ² | 1 | zDifAyErrC1}% and needed increase in tolerance based on the situation occurs, after a time of %{120 | ms | 0 | tayFV2Sw1*40}% the vehicle dynamic controller will disregard the sensor information so that a false vehicle dynamic intervention is prevented. During observability the recognition time depends on the amount of failure.The deviation of the measured signal from the model values is integrated when exceeding the allowed threshold. The shut down threshold for the fault integral IBeta is %{ 4.363 | 1/s | 2 | IBetaMax*(3.1416/180)/0.04 }% .During cornering only the fault integral increases, fault is only set during straight ahead driving.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_931180025">Huge tolerance in assembly position of the sensor or wrong wiring or internal offset or sensitivity fault of the sensor.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
