                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6581153</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C246BA1</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_376108138">wss undervoltage has been detected for FL wheel</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1985976417">Detection of the undervoltage situation is done with the System ASIC internal hardware comparator called K7. This comparator monitors the voltage between the WSS power supply line and WSS signal line. The monitoring threshold can be configured for Threshold A0 to A15 to match the power supply thresholds of the used WSS type. If the System ASIC is equipped with the boost converter, the power supply of the WSS is always sufficient.So failure reason ECU internal failure.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1485044085">If the System ASIC is equipped with the boost converter, the power supply of the WSS is always sufficient.ECU internal failure</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
