                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1376446618">The monitoring checks for a lost signal fault and consists of following parts: 1.) drive off low monitoring: The failure is set after a particular wheel speed stays at zero for a minimum time %{ 0.5 | s | 1 |   }% after drive off and afterwards the vehicle velocity increases by a specific threshold %{ 3.4 | m/s | 1 |   }%. The monitoring is able to detect up to two defect wheel speed sensors.2.) drive off high monitoring: The failure is set after a particular wheel speed drops to zero and the vehicle velocity increases by a specific threshold %{ 5 | m/s | 2 | MAX(MAX((SspWss_vDOLO_CheckFailLower*((48/2)/(AnzahlZaehne_VA/Abrollumfang_VA))),SspWss_vDOLO_CheckFailLower),SspWss_v_DOHI_Offset)}%. The monitoring is able to detect up to two defect wheel speed sensors.3.) dynamic monitoring: The failure is set after a particular wheel speed drops to zero and no edges of the encoding wheel are delivered by the sensor.From functional perspective, the monitoring shall not be curable within the same ignition cycle, although in DEM it is configured as curable. This is only implemented like this to be able to use DEM functionality "Sequential failure buffer" to synchronize with HSW WSS monitors. The monitor will never reset in the same cycle after a fault is detected without HSW fault detected.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_10085620">1.) The WSS is not correctly mounted, so that no signal is induced in sensor element. 2.) The WSS is dislodged from bracket, so that no signal is induced in sensor element.  3.) The airgap between sensor and encoding wheel is too big to induce sufficient signal in sensor element. 4.) Malfunction of sensor internal logic. 5.) Tone wheel not mounted correctly or demagnetized. 6.) The Input amplifier in ECU is faulty. 7.) The WSS signal is disturbed by loose contact. 8.) The WSS signal is disturbed by open circuit in the WSS line.</SD>
