                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1837033187">The failure is set if the difference between maximum and minimum wheel speed related to vehicle speed exceeds a calculated threshold. This threshold is depending on vehicle speed and current system mode. A wheel specific fault is set, if the faulty wheel is always the same. 1.) ESP Mode: For vehicle speeds lower than a specific value %{ 5.56 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_v_Switch5 }% the failure threshold is an absolute value %{ 1.4 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo5/SspWss_MonVdiff_v_SREF_perc }%. Above this vehicle speed the failure threshold is a relative value %{ 5 | % | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo5 }%. 2.) ABS and backup-EBD Mode: For vehicle speeds lower than a specific value %{ 27.8 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_v_Switch6 }% the failure threshold is an absolute value %{ 1.7 | m/s | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo6/SspWss_MonVdiff_v_SREF_perc }%. Above this vehicle speed the failure threshold is a relative value %{ 6 | % | 2 | SspWss_MonVdiff_vDiff_Lo6 }%.</SD>
